## Why This Is Asked
Tests encryption architecture, per-device keys, and offline synchronization with conflict resolution.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption
- Android Keystore key rotation
- Room encryption with per-note DEK
- CRDT tombstones and delta graphs
- GraphQL manifests for sync

## Code Example
```javascript
function rotateKEK(currentKEK, dekMap) {
  // re-wrap DEKs with new KEK, avoiding payload re-encryption
  const newDekMap = {};
  Object.entries(dekMap).forEach(([id, wrappedDek]) => {
    newDekMap[id] = wrapWithKEK(wrappedDek, currentKEK);
  });
  return newDekMap;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect and resolve diverging deltas from different devices?
- What failure modes affect encryption during rotation and how to test them?

